      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f01ee1248ee5765bbfc3a70|full_name}: The whole premise for this suggestion is that new people are always horrible and don't want genuine interactions, I think that's a dangerous mindset that only will only result in users having even more trouble integrating into the community than they already do and in the long run make VRchat more miserable for everyone playing.\nThe trust rank should only be used to personalize your own individual experience, not to be used as a means to \"prove your worth\" in any matter in terms of game functionality. What trust rank you have means nothing how you are as a person (With the exception of nuisance rank, of course...) A trusted user can be just as toxic, if not worse, than a visitor. You really don't know unless you actually talk with them so you should treat everyone as a individual. Not by their rank.\nFrom what I can gather you're actually just looking for a more curated way of meeting strangers that most likely won't be a complete dickhead, and there are many better suggestions for that without having to lock people out, like, \nBeing able to join and enter player group instances, which would be moderated by the group themselves, or being able to organize and join event instances from a in-game list. I think would do a much better job at filtering out trolls, as the organizers can just kick them if it becomes a problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
